<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nayapala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nayapala was a king of the Pala dynasty who reigned in the first half of the eleventh century, the son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahipala-i-pala">Mahipala I</a>. He fought the Kalachuri king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmikarna">Lakshmikarna</a>, and Tibetan tradition holds that the teacher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atisha">Atisha</a> helped make peace between them. Atisha's departure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramashila">Vikramashila</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> around 1040, during his reign, reflects the continuing prestige of the Pala monasteries.</p></div>
